From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: enable PLIC channels at the CPU through the mie CSR

The ESP32-C6 and ESP32-H2 deliver their PLIC channels through the core's
machine interrupt enable CSR: mie bit n gates channel n.  ESP-IDF raises
those bits in its ROM esprv_intc_int_enable(), which programs the PLIC
enable and the CPU side together.  The BSP programmed only the PLIC.

On the ESP32-H2 that masked every interrupt at the core while the PLIC
reported the channel as pending: the SYSTIMER target 0 alarm set INT_RAW,
the interrupt matrix routed source 45 to channel 16, the PLIC showed
channel 16 in EIP status with priority 15 above a threshold of 1, and the
core never took the trap.  The scheduler tick therefore never advanced and
rtems_task_wake_after() never returned.

Raise the mie bits together with the PLIC enable when the facility enables
all channels.

Signed-off-by: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
---
 bsps/riscv/esp32/irq/irq_c3.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/bsps/riscv/esp32/irq/irq_c3.c
+++ b/bsps/riscv/esp32/irq/irq_c3.c
@@ -428,6 +428,14 @@
 static inline void esp32_cpu_int_enable_all( void )
 {
   INTPRI_CPU_REG( 0x00 ) = 0xffffffffU;
+  /*
+   * The CPU side of the PLIC is the machine interrupt enable CSR: bit n
+   * gates channel n.  ESP-IDF's ROM esprv_intc_int_enable() raises the
+   * matching mie bits alongside the PLIC enable; programming only the PLIC
+   * leaves every channel asserted in EIP status and never delivered to the
+   * core, so no interrupt handler ever runs.
+   */
+  set_csr( mie, 0xffffffffU );
 }
 
 static inline void esp32_cpu_int_type_level( void )
